{
 "id": "20-01-four-bit-adder",
 "title": "Finish the 4-bit adder",
 "kind": "logic",
 "story": "This 4-bit ripple-carry adder is built from four full adders (each: two XOR, two AND, one OR), with the carry into bit 0 tied to 0. Three gates are missing: the sum gate of bit 1 (S1), the gate that passes the carry on in bit 2 (S2: it should be 1 only when exactly one of a2, b2 is 1 AND a carry comes in) and the generate gate of bit 3 (S3: it should be 1 when a3 and b3 are both 1). Fill them so the adder passes all 256 test sums, within 20 gates and a critical path of 9 gate delays.",
